<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index up 0.24 percent.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index up 0.24 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index rose 0.18 points, 0.24 percent, to 76.33 points after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index fell 41.72 points, 1.23 percent, to 3,349.82</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over the local market was 11.21 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove Index is a capitalisation weighted basket Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- David Chance, London newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
